winex11: don't turn a grab's crossing events into mouse input.

X11DRV_SetCursorPos grabs the pointer on root_window around XWarpPointer.
In a Wine virtual desktop root_window is the desktop's own X window, so
the grab sends that window an EnterNotify (mode NotifyGrab, detail
NotifyInferior) carrying the pointer position from *before* the warp.
The desktop's window belongs to explorer's thread, whose warp_serial
the warp never set, so is_old_motion_event() lets the event through and
X11DRV_EnterNotify sends the stale position as mouse input: the cursor
jumps back to where it was warped from. A program that warps the cursor
back to an anchor after each move (a 3D viewport's camera) then reads
every move twice. Measured with research/upstream-reports/camprobe.c
over VNC: a 40 px drag read as 70-79 px, exactly 40 with this.

A crossing caused by a grab or ungrab is not pointer motion; the motion
itself arrives as MotionNotify either way.

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/mouse.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/mouse.c
@@ -1652,6 +1652,13 @@
 
     if (hwnd == NtUserGetAncestor( get_capture_window(), GA_ROOT )) return FALSE;
 
+    /* A crossing caused by a grab is not pointer motion. */
+    if (event->mode == NotifyGrab || event->mode == NotifyUngrab)
+    {
+        TRACE( "pos %d,%d grab crossing, ignoring\n", event->x, event->y );
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+
     if (is_old_motion_event( event->serial ))
     {
         TRACE( "pos %d,%d old serial %lu, ignoring\n", event->x, event->y, event->serial );
